"""Run $name, in any of alhazen's six modes, on any rig.

    python run.py --task $task_name --mode demo      --rig configs/rig-mac.yaml
    python run.py --task $task_name --mode movie     --rig configs/rig-lab.yaml --out movies
    python run.py --task $task_name --mode measure   --rig configs/rig-lab.yaml
    python run.py --task $task_name --mode simulate  --rig configs/rig-lab.yaml --seed 1 --headless
    python run.py --task $task_name --mode test      --rig configs/rig-mac.yaml --sub dev --ses 1 --initials DEV
    python run.py --task $task_name                  --rig configs/rig-lab.yaml --sub s01 --ses 1 --initials AB

A rig file describes a machine; the mode decides what to do with it. So the
laptop config and the rig config each take all six modes — simulate stands
the rig's real devices down, test lets the mouse stand in for a tracker the
laptop does not have. The default rig is the laptop, so that
``python run.py --task $task_name --mode demo`` with no ``--rig`` shows the
stimulus wherever you are sitting.

Every command names the task, ``--task $task_name``, though this package has
only the one: every session alhazen starts names its task. Until alhazen 3.0
a command without it still runs $task_name and warns; 3.0 refuses it.
(``--mode measure`` checks the machine and runs no task, so it needs none.)

This exists so the experiment can be started without installing anything.
Once the package is installed (``pip install -e .``),
``alhazen run --task $task_name --rig <file>`` starts the same session
through the same code, because what else a session needs from this
experiment is declared on its task, which both are handed: the params file
(``default_params`` in src/$package/task.py, used when ``--params`` is not
given) and what the subject reads before trial one (``instructions``). The
one difference is the rig: this file starts on the laptop's by default, and
``alhazen run`` needs ``--rig``.

The argument parser, the run-number counter, the rehearsal path — everything
every experiment needs — is alhazen's ``run_experiment``. What belongs here
is only what is about THIS experiment and not already on its task: which
task it is, and which rig to start on.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import sys
from pathlib import Path

from alhazen.cli.modes import run_experiment

from $package.task import $task_class

HERE = Path(__file__).parent

if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(
        run_experiment(
            task_class=$task_class,
            default_rig=HERE / "configs" / "rig-mac.yaml",
            argv=sys.argv[1:],
        )
    )
